<article class="page-body">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Kiavi Requirements: What It Takes to Qualify</h1>
    <p class="lede">Kiavi's box is wide but specific. Here's the checklist before you spend time on an application — and the things Kiavi will <em>never</em> ask you for.</p>

    <h2>The requirements at a glance</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Kiavi's standard</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Credit score</td><td>~660 minimum FICO (higher improves pricing)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>None required — pricing tiers by exits in the last 24 months</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Loan size</td><td>~$100K minimum, up to ~$3M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Property type</td><td>Non-owner-occupied 1–4 unit residential: SFR, condos, townhomes, 2–4 units</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Occupancy</td><td>Investment only — never a primary residence</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Location</td><td>49 states + DC (not Utah); urban/suburban markets</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Entity</td><td>Most loans close in an LLC or corporation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Down payment</td><td>Bridge: as little as 5–10% of cost (up to 95% LTC); DSCR: typically 20–25% down</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>

    <h2>What Kiavi does NOT require</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No W-2s, pay stubs, or tax returns</strong> on bridge loans — there is no personal income check at all. Details: <a href="/faqs/does-kiavi-verify-income/">does Kiavi verify income?</a></li>
      <li><strong>No debt-to-income ratio.</strong> DSCR rentals qualify on the property's rent instead.</li>
      <li><strong>No hard credit pull to see pricing.</strong> The initial quote is a soft inquiry.</li>
      <li><strong>No prior flips required.</strong> First-timers qualify; they just don't get the floor rate (see <a href="/kiavi-rates/">rates</a>).</li>
    </ul>

    {% include "partials/cta.njk" %}

    <h2>DSCR-specific requirements</h2>
    <p>For the 30-year rental loan, Kiavi checks the <strong>debt-service-coverage ratio</strong>: market rent divided by the full monthly payment (principal, interest, taxes, insurance, HOA). A DSCR around 1.0–1.1 is generally the floor, 1.2+ gets better pricing, and leases or a market-rent appraisal document the income. More in <a href="/kiavi-dscr-loans/">our DSCR guide</a>.</p>

    <h2>Common disqualifiers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Property in Utah, rural property, mixed-use, or 5+ units</li>
      <li>Loan under ~$100K — see <a href="/faqs/kiavi-minimum-loan-amount/">minimum loan amount</a> for alternatives</li>
      <li>Owner-occupancy or intent to occupy</li>
      <li>FICO below ~660, or recent foreclosure/bankruptcy (seasoning required)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Qualify? Get the bonus too.</h2>
    <p>If you fit the box, apply through <a href="{{ site.affiliateLink }}" rel="sponsored noopener" target="_blank">the partner link</a> before you create an account — new customers get <strong>{{ site.offerAmount }} cash</strong> after the first loan closes, and it can't be added retroactively. <a href="/">How the bonus works</a>.</p>
